-- title:
--   Germ ideals under stalk maps: comap and kernel sheaves
-- statement:
--   The theorem takes no arguments: it asserts the conjunction of two universally quantified statements about ideal sheaf data on schemes. First, for all schemes $X, X'$ (in a fixed universe), every morphism $f : X' \to X$, every $I : X.\mathrm{IdealSheafData}$, every point $x'$ of $X'$, every affine open $U$ of $X$ with $f(x') \in U$, every affine open $U'$ of $X'$ with $x' \in U'$, and every proof that $U' \le f^{-1}U$: the ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X',x'}$ generated by the image, under the stalk map $\mathcal O_{X,f(x')} \to \mathcal O_{X',x'}$ of $f$ at $x'$, of the ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,f(x')}$ generated by the germs at $f(x')$ of the sections in $I.\mathrm{ideal}\,U \subseteq \Gamma(X,U)$, is contained in the ideal of $\mathcal O_{X',x'}$ generated by the germs at $x'$ of the sections in $(I.\mathrm{comap}\,f).\mathrm{ideal}\,U' \subseteq \Gamma(X',U')$. Second, for all schemes $C, X$, every morphism $\varphi : C \to X$, every point $c$ of $C$ and every affine open $U$ of $X$ with $\varphi(c) \in U$: the ideal of $\mathcal O_{C,c}$ generated by the image under the stalk map of $\varphi$ at $c$ of the ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,\varphi(c)}$ generated by the germs at $\varphi(c)$ of the sections in $\varphi.\mathrm{ker}.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ is the zero ideal.
--
--   These are the two pointwise (stalk-level) forms of functoriality for ideal sheaf data: compatibility of germ ideals with the pullback $I \mapsto I.\mathrm{comap}\,f$, and the vanishing at every stalk of the germ ideal of the kernel ideal sheaf of a morphism. They are used in the analysis of the local rings of the modular curve $X_1(p)$ at a crossing point, in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.isInvertible_comap_ker_and_comap_ker_eq_prod_ofPoint_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.isInvertible_comap_ker_and_comap_ker_eq_prod_ofPoint_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
